From a258ae7e8ce383011ed1ecc8b51bb804b18f7619 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:27:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(txn): free a child's remove event when the child
 aborts

DB_ENV->dbremove inside a child transaction queues a TXN_REMOVE event
on the child (__txn_remevent, from __db_inmem_remove or
__fop_ondisk_swap).  __txn_doevents hands a committing child's remove
event to its parent.  On abort it jumps straight to the free code
(dofree), which also kept a child's TXN_REMOVE event "for the parent",
but nothing had handed it over: the event, its name and file id were in
no list and leaked (6 blocks per in-memory remove, 5 on disk).

Keep the event only when a committing child handed it to its parent;
free it on abort.

Test: test/db/txn_remevent_leak.c counts every libdb allocation through
db_env_set_func_malloc/realloc/free (no leak detector needed): in-memory
and on-disk removes in a child, aborted via the parent or the child,
leak nothing; controls (commit through child and parent, top-level
abort, no remove) are unchanged and a committed remove still removes.

Found by dbsql (SQLite SAVEPOINT; DROP TABLE; ROLLBACK on :memory:).
---
 src/txn/txn_util.c               |   8 +-
 test/MANIFEST                    |   1 +
 test/db/run_txn_remevent_leak.sh |  91 ++++++++++++
 test/db/txn_remevent_leak.c      | 236 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 335 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100755 test/db/run_txn_remevent_leak.sh
 create mode 100644 test/db/txn_remevent_leak.c

diff --git a/src/txn/txn_util.c b/src/txn/txn_util.c
index c1ad42d9f..e29b1b752 100644
--- a/src/txn/txn_util.c
+++ b/src/txn/txn_util.c
@@ -371,7 +371,13 @@ dofree:
 		/* Free resources here. */
 		switch (e->op) {
 		case TXN_REMOVE:
-			if (txn->parent != NULL)
+			/*
+			 * On commit a child's remove event was handed to its
+			 * parent above, and is freed when the parent ends.  On
+			 * abort the jump here skipped that hand-off: the event
+			 * is in no list, so it must be freed now.
+			 */
+			if (txn->parent != NULL && opcode != TXN_ABORT)
 				continue;
 			if (e->u.r.fileid != NULL)
 				__os_free(env, e->u.r.fileid);
diff --git a/test/MANIFEST b/test/MANIFEST
index b46d23b97..909f14299 100644
--- a/test/MANIFEST
+++ b/test/MANIFEST
@@ -466,6 +466,7 @@ db	run_recd_compact
 db	run_recd_handlers
 db	run_upgrade
 db	run_lock_priority_nullderef
